```

## Supported Classes

### Emotions

- Angry
- Disgust
- Fear
- Happy
- Neutral
- Sad
- Surprise

### Gender

- Male
- Female

## Setup

### 1. Clone the repository

```bash
git clone https://github.com/Fs-ilm26/emotion-recognition-gender-classification.git
cd emotion-recognition-gender-classification
```

### 2. Create a virtual environment

```bash
python -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate   # Linux/macOS
# .venv\Scripts\activate    # Windows
```

### 3. Install dependencies

```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

## Dataset Preparation

The project expects image data in one of the following structures:

### Option A: Organize by emotion folders

```text
data/
├── train/
│   ├── angry/
│   ├── disgust/
│   ├── fear/
│   ├── happy/
│   ├── neutral/
│   ├── sad/
│   └── surprise/
└── validation/
    ├── angry/
    ├── disgust/
    ├── fear/
    ├── happy/
    ├── neutral/
    ├── sad/
    └── surprise/
```

For gender classification, the code can also use a metadata CSV file if available.

### Option B: Use a CSV annotation file

```text
data/metadata.csv
```

with columns like:

```csv
image_path,emotion,gender
train/angry/img1.jpg,angry,male
train/happy/img2.jpg,happy,female
```

## Training

Run:

```bash
python src/train.py
```

The training script:

- loads the dataset
- builds the shared CNN with dual-output heads
- trains emotion and gender classifiers together
- saves the best model to `models/emotion_gender_model.keras`
- saves evaluation metrics for later review

## Inference

### Single image

```bash
python src/inference.py --image path/to/image.jpg --model models/emotion_gender_model.keras
```

### Live camera feed

```bash
python src/live_demo.py --model models/emotion_gender_model.keras
```

## Model Architecture

The architecture is based on a shared convolutional feature extractor with two heads:

- shared CNN backbone: efficient visual feature learning
- emotion output head: Softmax over 7 classes
- gender output head: Sigmoid/Softmax over 2 classes

This structure allows the system to perform both tasks in a single pipeline while reducing redundant computation.

## Notes

This repository is intended to be easy to adapt for:

- FER (Facial Expression Recognition) datasets
- live camera classification
- real-time human interaction analysis
- edge deployment prototypes

## Dependencies

- TensorFlow / Keras
- OpenCV
- NumPy
- Matplotlib
- scikit-learn
- pandas

